|~ What is declared under `::boolean`: the refusal of its
   constructor, the negation, and the two combinators of conditions,
   which take booleans. ~|

:boolean/construct
  |~~ Reads a boolean as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:boolean/PayloadNotBooleanError
  |~~ `::boolean` reads its payload as the boolean it is; a payload of
      another kind is refused.
  ~~|

:boolean/PayloadNotBooleanError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number is no boolean and is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(::boolean(1) !| [type /actualType] | eq [::boolean/PayloadNotBooleanError ::number])

:boolean/not
  |~~ The negation of a boolean. Null is tested with `eq null`, and a
      subject of another kind is refused.

      `not` turns a boolean; a value is asked whether it is absent by
      `eq null`, and a container whether it is empty by `empty`.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:boolean/not/turnsFalseTrue
  |~~ Not false is true. ~~|
  ::law~(false | not | eq true)

:boolean/not/turnsTrueFalse
  |~~ Not true is false. ~~|
  ::law~(true | not | eq false)

:boolean/not/asksNullByEq
  |~~ Null is asked for by `eq null`, not by `not`. ~~|
  ::law~(null | eq null | eq true)

:boolean/not/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number is no boolean, and `not` refuses it. ~~|
  ::law~(0 | not !| [type /actualType] | eq [::boolean/not/SubjectNotBooleanError ::number])

:boolean/not/negation
  |~~ The other boolean. ~~|
  ::boolean

:boolean/and
  |~~ Whether the subject and the right condition both hold, each a
      boolean. Two conditions of one record hold together by `allOf`,
      `allOf /active (/age | gte 18)`, which composes the clauses of a
      predicate inside `filter`, `every` and `if`.

      The left condition of `and` must answer a boolean.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:boolean/and/isFalseWhenOneIsFalse
  |~~ True and false is false. ~~|
  ::law~(true | and false | eq false)

:boolean/and/holdsTwoConditionsByAllOf
  |~~ Two conditions of one record hold together by `allOf`. ~~|
  ::law~({:active true :age 25} | allOf /active (/age | gte 18) | eq true)

:boolean/and/failsWhenOneConditionFails
  |~~ `allOf` is false when one condition is. ~~|
  ::law~({:active false :age 25} | allOf /active (/age | gte 18) | eq false)

:boolean/and/refusesASubjectOfAnotherKind
  |~~ A subject that is no boolean is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(1 | and true !| [type /actualType] | eq [::boolean/and/SubjectNotBooleanError ::number])

:boolean/and/right
  |~~ The condition on the right.

      The right condition of `and` must answer a boolean.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:boolean/and/right/refusesARightOfAnotherKind
  |~~ A right condition that is no boolean is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(true | and 1 !| [type /actualType] | eq [::boolean/and/right/NotBooleanError ::number])

:boolean/and/right/NotBooleanError
  |~~ The right is a boolean. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::boolean)

:boolean/and/both
  |~~ Whether the subject and the other condition both hold. ~~|
  ::boolean

:boolean/or
  |~~ Whether the subject or the right condition holds, each a boolean.
      Conditions of one subject hold by one of them through `anyOf`,
      `5 | anyOf (eq 5) (eq 10)`.

      The left condition of `or` must answer a boolean.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:boolean/or/isTrueWhenOneIsTrue
  |~~ False or true is true. ~~|
  ::law~(false | or true | eq true)

:boolean/or/holdsByAnyOfOneCondition
  |~~ `anyOf` holds when one condition of the subject holds. ~~|
  ::law~(5 | anyOf (eq 5) (eq 10) | eq true)

:boolean/or/failsWhenNoConditionHolds
  |~~ `anyOf` is false when no condition holds. ~~|
  ::law~(7 | anyOf (eq 5) (eq 10) | eq false)

:boolean/or/readsTheFieldsOfARecord
  |~~ `anyOf` reads its conditions on the fields of a record. ~~|
  ::law~({:role "admin"} | anyOf (/role | eq "admin") (/role | eq "owner") | eq true)

:boolean/or/refusesASubjectOfAnotherKind
  |~~ A subject that is no boolean is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(1 | or true !| [type /actualType] | eq [::boolean/or/SubjectNotBooleanError ::number])

:boolean/or/right
  |~~ The condition on the right.

      The right condition of `or` must answer a boolean.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:boolean/or/right/refusesARightOfAnotherKind
  |~~ A right condition that is no boolean is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(false | or 1 !| [type /actualType] | eq [::boolean/or/right/NotBooleanError ::number])

:boolean/or/right/NotBooleanError
  |~~ The right is a boolean. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::boolean)

:boolean/or/either
  |~~ Whether the subject or the other condition holds. ~~|
  ::boolean
